---
import { techStack } from '../data/techStack';
---

<section id="about" class="bg-canvas border-t border-hairline py-section px-6">
  <div class="max-w-content mx-auto">

    {/* Section Header */}
    <div class="pb-3 mb-8 border-b border-hairline">
      <h2 class="text-heading-md text-ink">About Me</h2>
    </div>

    <div class="grid md:grid-cols-2 gap-12">
      {/* Text Content */}
      <div class="space-y-4">
        <p class="text-sm text-body leading-relaxed">
          I'm a frontend developer based in Yogyakarta, Indonesia. I started in 2020 as a vocational school intern building responsive pages for a social web app, and have worked mostly on the front end since, from a university study program platform to a large-scale enterprise platform today.
        </p>
        <p class="text-sm text-body leading-relaxed">
          I turn complex workflows into structured front ends: a BPMN process editor, a dynamic form builder, and a micro-frontend setup that lets many developers work in separate repos while the project stays maintainable. I also maintain a shared UI component library.
        </p>
        <p class="text-sm text-body leading-relaxed">
          I care about clean code, modular UI and developer experience, which in practice means shared components, written front-end standards and code quality checks with SonarCloud. Lately I've been exploring how applications and LLMs fit together and building products on top of them, from structured output and tool calling to UI the model can drive. BPMN AI Studio is the first of those. I write about what I learn along the way.
        </p>
      </div>

      {/* Tech Stack — list-row style */}
      <div>
        <h3 class="text-sm font-bold text-ink mb-4">Tech Stack</h3>
        <div class="border-t border-hairline">
          {techStack.map((tech) => (
            <div class="flex items-center gap-3 py-2 border-b border-hairline">
              <span class="text-xs text-mute">[+]</span>
              <span class="text-sm text-ink">{tech}</span>
            </div>
          ))}
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>

  </div>
</section>
